{:fh/id  "FH-CTRL-016"
 :fh/law "The first-party controls read ONE LEAF and there is no spelling that reads a container: neither has a `:value` prop, the only value either accepts is a leaf projection carrying its own path, and a caller's forwarded attributes go through the `v/spread-safe` deny law, which refuses `value` on the component's own controlled element in every build. The call site is one projection and one intent; the element they render is a native `<input>` carrying `value` with a literal event vector at `onInput`, which is the shape the controlled-input door recognises; and both declarations are inside the compiled grammar as they stand, so promotion is a keyword rather than a rewrite."

 :baseline {:contact {:email "a@b.c" :phone "555"}}

 :email-path [:contact :email]
 :phone-path [:contact :phone]

 :edit-intent  [:editor/edited  [:contact :email]]
 :visit-intent [:editor/visited [:contact :email]]

 ;; WHAT THE CONTROL RENDERS. One `:input`, its value taken from the leaf
 ;; projection, its `:on-input` the caller's intent completed with the
 ;; scalar projection the door fills.
 :tag :input
 :rendered-value "a@b.c"
 :rendered-on-input [:editor/edited [:contact :email] :re-frame.freehand/value]
 :rendered-on-blur  [:editor/visited [:contact :email]]

 ;; The blur is OPTIONAL: a form with no reveal-on-blur policy does not
 ;; have to invent an event to satisfy a component, and the element it
 ;; renders carries no blur at all.
 :on-blur-when-absent nil

 ;; A caller's ordinary attributes reach the element.
 :forwarded {:type "email" :class "input" :data-test "email"}

 ;; THE DENY. A caller who reaches for the container spelling has nowhere
 ;; to put it: `value` in the forwarded map is refused, loudly, by the one
 ;; deny law every component library forwards through.
 :denied-caller-prop :value
 :deny-error-id      :rf.error/ui-tree-malformed

 ;; NARROWNESS, proven as a VALUE fact rather than asserted as a hope. A
 ;; keystroke in one leaf leaves the OTHER leaf's projection byte
 ;; identical, so a subscription over it publishes nothing and the sibling
 ;; control does not re-render inside the keystroke.
 :typed-in-email "mike@example.com"

 ;; …while the CONTAINER read — the spelling this API has no room for —
 ;; changes on the very same keystroke. Both halves are asserted, because
 ;; "the narrow read did not change" is only interesting beside "the wide
 ;; read did".
 :container-read-changes? true
 :leaf-read-changes?      false

 ;; THE COMPILED TIER. Both declarations are checked, as they stand, by
 ;; the analyzer the build runs — eligible, with nothing to change on the
 ;; way.
 :view-ids [:re-frame.freehand.controls/field
            :re-frame.freehand.controls/buffered-field]
 :compile-eligible? true
 :findings []
 :current-lowering :interpreted}
